# Inventory-Led Meta Ads Campaign Execution System — 25% Off Storewide

---

# Project Overview

## Project Name
Inventory-Led Meta Advertising & Campaign Optimization System

## Industry
D2C Ecommerce — Kids Fashion

## Teams Involved
- Marketing Operations Team
- Meta Ads Team
- Listing Team
- Inventory Operations Team
- Website/Product Feed Team

---

# Project Objective

Build a synchronized inventory-driven Meta advertising workflow where:
- inventory availability
- sales velocity
- marketplace demand
- category performance
- product sizing
- advertising spend

all work together to optimize:
- ad spend efficiency
- conversion rates
- inventory movement
- discounting strategy
- campaign targeting
- sales velocity

The project focused on aligning operational inventory data with Meta campaign execution for a “25% Off Storewide” sale campaign.

---

# Business Problem

The business faced several operational and advertising challenges:

- ad budgets were being spent on low-stock products
- customers clicked ads only to find sizes unavailable
- inventory movement was uneven across categories
- high-stock products required faster sales velocity
- ad teams lacked real-time inventory visibility
- marketplace and DTC prioritization were not synchronized

This resulted in:
- wasted ad spend
- lower conversion rates
- higher bounce rates
- inefficient inventory liquidation
- poor campaign prioritization

---

# Solution Approach

A coordinated operational and advertising roadmap was designed where:
- inventory data guided ad spend allocation
- category-level sales data determined campaign priority
- size-level availability influenced ad messaging
- low-stock SKUs were dynamically excluded
- marketing and operations teams synchronized daily

